deKorator - themable window decoration for KDE Plasma 6
=======================================================

This is the Plasma 6 (Qt 6 / KDE Frameworks 6 / KDecoration3) port of
deKorator. For the history of the project see README.original and ChangeLog.

Requirements
------------

- Qt >= 6.6 (Core, DBus, Gui, Widgets)
- KDE Frameworks >= 6.5 (Archive, Config, CoreAddons, I18n, IconThemes,
  KCMUtils, KIO, NewStuff, WidgetsAddons, XmlGui) and extra-cmake-modules
- KDecoration3 (Plasma 6.3 or later)

Building and installing
-----------------------

    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
    cmake --build build
    sudo cmake --install build

Then restart KWin (log out and back in, or run "kwin_wayland --replace &"
on Wayland) and choose "DeKorator" in System Settings > Colors & Themes >
Window Decorations. The pencil/configure button opens the deKorator
settings, where themes are selected, installed from archives, or downloaded
with "Get New Themes...".

Installed files:

- lib/qt6/plugins/org.kde.kdecoration3/org.kde.deKorator.so  (decoration)
- lib/qt6/plugins/org.kde.kdecoration3.kcm/kcm_deKoratordecoration.so  (settings)
- share/deKorator/themes/Default-theme  (the default theme)
- share/knsrcfiles/deKoratorthemes.knsrc

Themes
------

Themes are looked up in deKorator/themes below the XDG data directories,
i.e. ~/.local/share/deKorator/themes and /usr/share/deKorator/themes. More
themes are in themesStuff/. If the configured theme cannot be found (for
example with a config file from KDE 4) the Default theme is used.

Settings are stored in ~/.config/kwindeKoratorrc, with the same keys as in
KDE 4, so an old configuration can be copied over.

Changes compared to the KDE 4 version
-------------------------------------

- "Close window by double clicking the menu button" is now the global
  KWin setting (Window Decorations > Titlebar Buttons), so the deKorator
  option is hidden.
- The pointing hand cursor over buttons is no longer supported, KDecoration3
  has no API for decoration cursors.
- Corner masks are implemented by clipping the painting, so masked corners
  are transparent (needs compositing, which is always on in Plasma 6).
- The window tab close button is gone, Plasma 6 has no window tabs.
- The "Blend" and "Solarize" button animations work again (they were
  disabled in the KDE 4 port), and QImageBlitz is no longer needed.
